# Chloroform (CHCl3): gas-phase XTB2 geometry optimization
# Purpose:
#   Cheap semiempirical (XTB2) gas-phase Opt of a single chloroform molecule,
#   analogous to the water/DMSO/MeOH gas-phase XTB2 Opts (water/XTB2,
#   DMSO/XTB2, MeOH/XTB2), for later comparison/reference alongside the
#   Apixaban SMD(chloroform) work (Apixaban/Chloroform).
#
# Starting geometry: idealized tetrahedral CHCl3 geometry (approximate C-H =
#   1.09 Ang, C-Cl = 1.77 Ang, close to tetrahedral angles) - a rough starting
#   guess only; XTB2 will relax bond lengths/angles to their true values.

! XTB2 Opt

* xyz 0 1
C    0.00000   0.00000   0.00000
H    0.00000   0.00000   1.09000
Cl   1.66640   0.00000  -0.58880
Cl  -0.83290   1.44280  -0.58880
Cl  -0.83290  -1.44280  -0.58880
*
